title: The Independents Mediate
subtitle: Kautsky and Breitscheid go between the Chancellery and the Committee.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: crisis_january = 1 and crisis_time = 1
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.e19_noske += 2;
Q.crisis_line_2 = 'Noske\'s volunteers: ' + Q.e19_noske + ',000, at Dahlem';
!}

= The Independents Mediate

For two days the Independents have carried messages between the two sides. The government will talk about nothing until the newspaper buildings are cleared. The Committee will clear nothing until Eichhorn is back. On 8 January the government's proclamation says: "The hour of reckoning is near." Noske is drilling his volunteers in Dahlem.

[? if e19_talks = 1 : Our delegates are at the table, and the men in the buildings do not trust them. ?][? if jan_line = 1 : We have said there is nothing to negotiate. ?]

- @pledge: Give up three of the buildings as a pledge.
- @eichhorn: Talk, but give up nothing until Eichhorn is restored.
- @break: Break off the talks.

@pledge
subtitle: Fewer buildings to defend, and the Independents will speak for the rest.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e19_buildings -= 3;
Q.e19_talks = 1;
Q.lean_unionist += 1;
Q.ultraleft_satisfaction -= 6;
Q.crisis_line_1 = 'Buildings held: ' + Q.e19_buildings + ' of 6';
!}

The occupiers of Mosse, Ullstein and Scherl march out with their rifles and go home. *Vorwärts* and the others stay.

@eichhorn
subtitle: A demand every worker understands. The government will refuse it.
on-arrival: lean_luxemburgist += 1; uspd_relation += 3

The government refuses. At least the factories can see who refused.

@break
subtitle: The occupiers want it. Noske will come sooner.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e19_talks = 0;
Q.e19_arms += 1;
Q.e19_noske += 1;
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
Q.uspd_relation -= 5;
Q.crisis_line_2 = 'Noske\'s volunteers: ' + Q.e19_noske + ',000, at Dahlem';
!}

The Committee sends the mediators home. In the *Vorwärts* building the men stack sandbags at the windows.
